hings like that i have to think  that the production team prefers to  treat cast members like  some kind of farm animal for her own  sick  viewing pleasure rather than as  dignified  human beings who deserve to be treated  with empathy and respect  i'm trying not to get worked up here but  let's close off on number five  that it positions weight loss surgery as  a quick fix  now there's no denying that weight loss  surgery can be a viable solution for  folks  who are struggling with obesity as  research has consistently shown  that it can help patients lose anywhere  between 50  and 70 of their excess weight and when  it comes to individuals with morbid  obesity  surgery can certainly make all of the  difference to improve  not only the physical and metabolic  consequences  of obesity but also improving their  overall quality of life  and we've seen just how impactful  bariatric surgery can be  in the lives of those featured in the  where are they now  series so let's take a quick look  everything about my life is better  mentally physically emotionally just a  different person now  so i'm completely focused on making more  and more progress  so of course this is really encouraging  to see however it's important to note  that  weight loss surgery is not a one-stop  shop for long-term weight loss  and it's not without its risks i talk  about this in depth in my video on  weight loss surgery risks and benefits  right here  but to recap the rate of weight loss  tends to decline  a year or so post-op while other  patients may  actually experience a lot of weight  regain one study found that the weight  regain rate was around 14  5 years post-op and that 40 of patients  maintained  at least 30 percent of their weight loss  after 12 years  just 40 percent now in addition  weight loss surgery may also cause major  complications  and nutritional risks so clearly this is  not a perfect  one and done procedure it's also  important to note that weight loss  surgery is not  brain surgery so if the underlying  psychological issues are  not addressed before and after surgery  the risks may  actually outweigh the benefits and put  someone on the path to  regaining the weight right back while  the show has only  now begun to mildly emphasize the  importance of therapeutic work  while also prescribing diets and  exercise regimens  i just want to strongly emphasize that  there is no  quick fix for weight loss whether that's  surgery  a crash diet or otherwise unfortunately  for most people  casually watching a 30 minute program  it might appear that to be the case my  hope is that the producers  at my 600 pound life will take the cast  members health  and well-being just as seriously if not  more seriously than tv ratings and views  morbid obesity is a serious condition  with very serious consequences  and should absolutely not be exploited  and on that note that is all that i have  for you guys today folks  thank you again to buildbar for  sponsoring this video  if you liked it be sure to give it the  thumbs up  leave me a comment below about what  you'd like to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen  bye
 

